From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Amaan Qureshi <git@amaanq.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 23:53:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] tabgroups: per-group container storage isolation

A shared default jar lets sites correlate otherwise separate tab groups.
Each group therefore keeps an on-disk StoragePartition keyed by its stable
group token. Group deletion is journaled before clearing and retried after a
crash, while Clear Browsing Data waits for every registered group partition.
Child creation follows the tab model grouping decision, while fixed siteless
SiteInstances retain the requested partition across chrome-native commits.
